      "slug": "yu-xiang",
      "term": "Yu Xiang",
      "definition": "A Sichuanese flavour profile meaning fish fragrant. It contains garlic, ginger, spring onion, chilli, vinegar, and sugar, but no fish. The name refers to the seasonings traditionally used with fish."
    },
    {
      "slug": "aubergine-salting",
      "term": "Salting Aubergine",
      "definition": "Cutting aubergine and tossing with salt to draw out moisture. This prevents the aubergine from absorbing too much oil during cooking and speeds up the cooking time."
    },
    {
      "slug": "stir-fry-seasoning",
      "term": "Seasoning Order",
      "definition": "In Chinese stir-frying, aromatics go in before vegetables, and sauce goes in last. This sequence builds flavour in stages and prevents the sauce from over-reducing."
    }
  ],
