            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "glossaryTooltip",
                "attrs": {
                  "termSlug": "yu-xiang"
                }
              }
            ],
            "text": "yu xiang"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " sauce. The combination of garlic, ginger, chilli, vinegar, and sugar was historically used to cook fish, and those same aromatics now define a whole class of Sichuanese vegetable dishes. Aubergine is the best vehicle for this sauce because its soft, absorbent texture soaks up every element."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Start with "
